A||||13||RiceCooker||A very meaningful poem - Opinions?||||1||
Z||000000||RiceCooker||12-05-2000||05:56 PM||||This might not be in everyone's department but if you want to read a mushy poem, please let me know what you think it means, why, any other thoughts, etc.<BR>Thanks<P>HIDDEN<P>		*I*nside a heart that’s blue<BR>		*L*ie feelings that are true<P>Hidden in the skies above, hidden in the trees<BR>Hidden from my future was what I could not read<BR>Oblivious then, to how great life could feel<BR>Hidden Deep inside my youth was all that I did bleed<P>		*O*ften scared, sometimes queezy<BR>	*V*oyages indeed, are not easy<P>Hidden in the skies above, hidden in the trees<BR>Hidden from all my life was what she brought to me<BR>She showed me who I was, made me who I am<BR>Hidden from her own two eyes is everything I need<P>		*E*motions pour out of this open heart<BR>	*Y*ou may want a brand new start<P>Hidden in the skies above, hidden in the trees<BR>Hidden from all the world is the way she smiles at me<BR>She is my passion, my courage, my fire<BR>Hidden from my own two eyes is how much in her I see<P>		*O*ne thing must be said, Deep, Honest, Pure, and True<BR>	*U*s is what matters, That’s why………….<P>Hidden in the skies above, hidden in the trees<BR>Hidden from reality is what we want to be<BR>So many dreams, much to do, it seems so far away<BR>Hidden from both our hearts is what destiny will be<P>The letters between the stars are supposed to be very large so they spell something downwards to fill in the blank (duh. It's really obvious with the big letters so I would have had to explain it)<BR>This poem is pretty thick so feel free to read it more than once.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by RiceCooker (edited 12-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||btoth||12-05-2000||07:42 PM||||Well, I'm not very good at analyzing poetry but I do find it interesting.  My girlfriend writes poetry all the time.. really deep stuff.<P>Do you already know what it's about?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I think part of it's about having a child and being able to see the world from a different perspective. (Am I close??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)  I'm sure that it's more involved than that though, hope someone else responds 'cause now I'm curious.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||RiceCooker||12-05-2000||08:56 PM||||It could be someone expressing/renewing his love for his other. Maybe he is reminding her of everything she is to him because they are in a hump in their relationship or something. Their future may seem uncertain and these are all of these hidden things - those that we never know about.<BR>Ask your gf what she thinks about it?||||reg||1
Z||000003||PearlBlueSoul||12-06-2000||04:10 AM||||That was very, Very good.  couldn't help but think how it paralleled several different things I'd written.  Correct me if I'm wrong, but, is it about a blind person?<P>mind if I add one to the list from me?<P>Dan Shaw<BR>12-7-99<BR>poems<P>Time can't let go<P>I can only think of you<BR>when I'm going through my day<BR>thinking about the blue<BR>and wondering how we will pay<P>thinking about you <BR>only brings deep regret<BR>but I love to tourture myself on you<BR>because I can't ever forget<P>I want to go away<BR>some place where I can hide<BR>I want to get away<BR>just crawl into a hole and open wide<P>let every tear and yell<BR>just flow out like waterfalls<BR>never think to stop the well<BR>of pain I see in the walls<P>inside my heart are built<BR>a dozen chambers each unique<BR>I ponder each one like a patch on a quilt<BR>some current and some antique<P>I can't help but stop<BR>to the one I made for you<BR>so intricate when the thought did pop<BR>into my head without a hint of blue<P>but now you've been torn out<BR>and the room has been blown apart<BR>this relationship has run out<BR>and I don't know where to start<P>the cleanup is so painful<BR>memories stab from every side<BR>where did I go wrong to have you become spiteful<BR>and then leave me without a ride<P>I don't know where things left<BR>I feel like I'm about to die<BR>as I pick up the only picture of us left<BR>I just begin to cry<P>I can't stop thinking of you<BR>even though you are gone<BR>I don't ever want to forget the sky so blue<BR>I shared while we were one<P>I don't want to forget everything we did<BR>the kisses we shared so sweet<BR>I never want to forget those things se said<BR>when the love stood tall on its feet.<P><BR>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">        <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.<p>[This message has been edited by PearlBlueSoul (edited 12-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||RiceCooker||12-06-2000||02:51 PM||||extremely touching PBS.<BR>I find that I can relate a lot to that just within the last couple of days.<BR>They've been pretty rough.<P>And yes, I did write that first poem.<P>The first 4liner is about how my life was empty before and I didn't know what lied ahead.<BR>"Hidden from her own two eyes is everything i need" describes how we both take for granted how much we mean to each other. <BR> "Hidden from my own two eyes is how much in her I see" means that maybe I do not show enough of my appreciation for everything she strives for. <BR>"Hidden from both our hearts is what destiny will be" describes how unsure both of us are about the future. <P>Did you get the fill in the blank part?<BR>How the two liners spell I Love You to complete the rhyme after "that's why...."<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT Bastard||12-06-2000||09:47 PM||||RiceCooker, that poem is f*cking ingenious.  Really.  PBS, I thought yours was put together really well too.  I can admire structured poetry such as that, although I prefer free-form poetry.  It just feels less restrictive, and I don't end up putting words together just because they rhyme.  Give it a try sometime.  I write some poetry occasionally, but I'm focusing on a screenplay right now(like everyone else..hehe)  Nice work.||||reg||1
Z||000006||PearlBlueSoul||12-06-2000||10:09 PM||||I see...that one you kind of have to have been there before.  Sorry to say I wouldn't know that feeling.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P><BR>I have tried freewriting.  lemme snag something real quick....<P>here's one I found (that was good enough to post).<P>Dan Shaw<BR>The Most Bitter Pill<P>The most bitter pill<BR>Is the one of truth<BR>When you know you’ve messed up<BR>And you have to take it in stride<P>You can’t refute it<BR>Because truth is fact<BR>And neither can you ignore it<BR>Because it will always come back<P>So you’re forced to make <BR>A decision whilst in a mixture<BR>Of hate, anger, sadness, and guilt<BR>Which makes it nearly impossible to see<P>What you’re supposed to do<BR>What you should do<BR>The options laid out to pick from<BR>So you can pick the path to take<P>It’s so ****in’ hard<BR>To really pick the right one<BR>When your soul is bangin’ around inside<BR>And it doesn’t want to settle down<P>It can’t be tamed<BR>Unless you release it through the fist<BR>Or the mouth that does more damage sometimes<BR>And never can be fixed<P>Or there’s the road of darkness<BR>Where you become scared and gray<BR>Of all the things you’ve thought<BR>As you fumbled in the fray<P>You know it will never last<BR>You know it will die soon<BR>But even though you know these things<BR>It is hell to go through<P>It takes forever it seems<BR>For sleep to erase the stray marks<BR>To make it partially disappear<BR>Just lessen the intensity<P>Never fear while this carries on<BR>For it won’t live long<BR>Just give it one good night’s rest<BR>And it will be exercised and gone<P><p>[This message has been edited by PearlBlueSoul (edited 12-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||PearlBlueSoul||12-06-2000||10:12 PM||||here's something else, albeit still a rhyme and an experiment on another type of style. I've tried to find a style that I like alot and it seems to be I can flow easily with 4 line sonnets that rhyme at lines 2 and 4.  <P>Dan Shaw<BR>Parallels<BR>12-13-99<P><BR>It should seem that things were never the same<BR>once the mind began work upon its game<P>Things of this world begin to coincide<BR>to the things that my mind provide<P>sad things equaled so true<BR>so sad when the sky is so blue<P>perfect days roll by fast<BR>never taking a look to see what they've passed<P>seeing me in the same shell<BR>living through the same twisted hell<P>and I listen to the world's cry<BR>to which I respond when my own soul doth die<P>it cremates itself time folded time<BR>when from out of a lip comes an equal rhyme<P>songs are the worst offenders to this extreme<BR>when within the mind oozes out a bloody cream<P>pain is the equal to the lyrical song<BR>when from out of the pain comes a lyric so long<P>so true to the feelings coming from within<BR>the sadness equals what the song contains again<P>it speaks the words the mind looses fast<BR>and echoes back the days gone past<P>for when times are at their worst and the brain can't save face<BR>the song can come quickly and keep up the time's pace<P>no matter how fast time thinks it runs<BR>it always sees upon its heels that of the lyric puns<P>for when you think things cannot get worse<BR>something comes along and explains it in verse<P>you listen although it deepens the gash<BR>but when you know what you deal with you can heal it's crash<P>song is the panacea for any crime within<BR>that either is thought, or physically is in<P>it cannot however cure the disease you bear<BR>but it gives you a point to think on and stare.||||reg||1
Z||000008||RiceCooker||12-07-2000||01:35 PM||||Thanks for listening guys.<BR>We were best friends also so it's like there aren't many people I can talk to.<P>My girlfriend and I of three years have just split. Those who have felt this pain can understand. For those who haven't it is unexplainable and I wouldn't wish it on my worst enemy. I can't eat or sleep. I've lost ten pounds in three days and it's not like I don't want to eat.<P>Sorry for being depressing but I guess that poem was one of the only things that made me feel any better.<BR>I will tell more if anyone else wants to hear it or shares a similar experience.  <P>"If you love something, let it go<BR>If it comes back then it's yours,<BR>If it doesn't, it never was."<BR>-Author Unknown<P>Later, Todd||||reg||9
Z||000009||Richard Parnell||12-07-2000||02:29 PM||||It was good to read your writings. I feel for you.<BR>I am also parting from someone that I have been with for 32 years.  I still love her but I guess I poisoned things by not being there when I should have been.  It's a sad lesson learned too late.||||reg||9
